~ The Deep Yards ~

[picture pic00]
[music lift]
At the far end of the freight lines,
past the last lamp, a cage lift hangs
over a shaft that goes down further than
the Waystation does. A brass plate on
the gate says YARD 48213. Someone has
scratched a number under it: 10.

The operator, a man made mostly of rust
and patience, doesn't look up. "Ten
floors," he says. "Every one a different
place. Come back up when you like. If
you can."

1. Step into the cage
2. Not today
> 1

The cage grinds down and stops. Floor 1.

[music bone]
A cathedral of bone where trains are
worshipped. A choir hums the timetable.

Ahead, past the buffers, a stair goes
down, and something is waiting by it.

1. A brazier, and an empty bench
2. Take the stairs down
3. Ride the cage back up
> 1

You sit by the brazier a while. Nobody
comes. It's the best kind of nobody.

The cage grinds down and stops. Floor 1.

A cathedral of bone where trains are
worshipped. A choir hums the timetable.

Ahead, past the buffers, a stair goes
down, and something is waiting by it.

1. Take the stairs down
